<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bemoim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1490</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as João Bemoim</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bemoim was a prince of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jolof-empire">Jolof Empire</a> in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> who ruled for a time before being driven out in a succession struggle. In 1488 he went to Portugal to seek help from King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-ii-of-portugal">João II</a>, was baptised with the king as his godfather and took the name João. He returned to Senegal with a Portuguese fleet that was to build a fort, but was killed by its commander, Pero Vaz da Cunha, on the voyage.</p></div>
